  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/1F2E92">Lemma <span data-tag="1F2E92">5.5.8.11</span>.</a> Let $K$ be a sifted simplicial set. Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-category which admits finite products and $K$-indexed colimits, and suppose that the formation of products in $\calX $ preserves $K$-indexed colimits separately in each variable. Then the colimit functor $\colim : \Fun (K, \calX ) \rightarrow \calX $ preserves finite products. </p>
